    "reader_path": [
      "The Gauduchon threefold mass polynomial becomes the elliptic fiber Dirichlet energy.",
      "The radial--vertical Schur complement isolates mixed derivatives.",
      "Gaussian heat potentials give logarithmic energy and a completed-square gradient estimate.",
      "A variable heat time and small integrated defect allow a base correction preserving positivity.",
      "Angular density comparison extends the same family to every scalar Hopf dimension at least three.",
      "Returning to H3, fiber averaging and the sharp Poincare inequality characterize bounded minimum mass.",
      "U(2)-invariant normalized potentials have a positive unit flux, yielding exact square-root damping conditions.",
      "Faster heat concentration separates individual finiteness, uniform deep tails and capacity continuity.",
      "Shrinking defects have horizontal closed quadratic currents and are exactly lifts of base measures.",
      "Changing the threefold Hermitian metric replaces Haar probabilities by its normalized fiber areas."
    ],
    "actual_editorial_concerns": [
      "The single long opening blends the mass counterexample, averaging, symmetry-dependent damping and general-metric shrinking defects.",
      "Retain normalization and the exact U(2) action in the symmetry-dependent regime.",
      "The general optimal damping rate and general-manifold defect-realization question remain open.",
      "Three short statement blocks split before their conclusion in the first compiled output; three local Needspace guards are added after actual full-page inspection.",
      "A final general-gap paragraph occupies a page by itself. Its substantive open-scope sentences move to the defect-section opening; the repeated special-classification recap is removed.",
      "Visible-heading/page-label comparison across all 28 Chapter 8 statement labels detects the sharp damping theorem label on 306 although its heading is on 307. A fourth local guard repairs the anchor and all 28 then match."
    ],
    "first_use_and_setting_map": [
      "X is first defined in the unbounded-mass theorem; omega, alpha, beta and s follow in the first section.",
      "The elliptic fiber E, lattice Lambda, Haar dA_E and projective base measure are defined before the energy formula.",
      "x and mu are declared in the radial frame; F_eta, heat time t and eta are declared before all scale calculations.",
      "Higher dimensions introduce H_n, alpha_n, beta_n and omega_n, then the root explicitly returns to X=H3.",
      "The rotational input retains the threefold and declares the U(2) action, normalized class R, W, Q_T and capacity.",
      "The shrinking input defines the fiberwise lift, arbitrary metric Omega, exact target mass b and quantified shrinking defect before use."
    ],
